;; spec:   stdlib §4.5 row merge-with ((merge-with f m1 m2 ..)), tranche 2 plan Y5 ("more maps are a user's reduce")
;; expect: reject
;; error:  merge-with takes 3 argument(s), got 4
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: merge-with
;; Y5's merge-with is a function of a combiner and two maps; Clojure's takes any number, and the library has no macro that
;; nests more (the plan leaves them to a user's reduce, as (reduce (fn (a m) (merge-with + a m)) a more)). So a third map
;; is the compile error above, never a silent drop of the third. The day a variadic macro lands this case is changed with it.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (count (merge-with + {1 2} {1 3} {2 4})))
